Findings (2)

  HIGH    ES008 Lossy bitmap or heavy recheck
          Bitmap Heap Scan on orders kept only page numbers for 1,549 of 2,081 pages, so it
          rechecked every row on them.
          Heap blocks: 1,549 lossy, 532 exact
          Rows removed by the recheck: 14,472
          Time in the node: 29.2 ms (49% of the runtime)
          → Raise work_mem for this query so that the bitmap stays exact.

  MEDIUM  ES013 Planner settings force the plan
          The plan was made with enable_indexscan = off and enable_seqscan = off, which keep the
          planner from some of its usual choices.
          Settings: enable_indexscan = off, enable_seqscan = off
          → Applications that plan with the defaults may get another plan: reset them (RESET
          enable_indexscan; RESET enable_seqscan, or a new session) and run EXPLAIN again. If a role
          or a database sets them (ALTER ROLE or ALTER DATABASE … SET), every session plans this
          way; to test a plan, SET LOCAL keeps a setting to one transaction.

Share and Time: time spent in each node itself, wall-clock. Rows: actual rows per loop, ×loops when
it ran more than once. ▲/▼: actual rows above or below the estimate by 10× or more. Buffers: pages
each node read itself.
